ry emits no stance line, while convergence emits one fixed stance line after the range and refuses a narrow scope or unknown stance before writing a brief. An ordinary review reading scope reads the delegated-decisions record and filed plan critiques, while a convergence scope excludes both; a convergence render refuses a reviewer template whose reading-scope command does not carry the review-record exclusion exactly once. The scope critique names the component and interface registries, derived architecture, runtime flows, and dependency ledger, marking an absent registry; the single-plan brief and scope critique render their registry lines from one declared set. A plan critique ties every severity class to a normal-use-reachable defect: a fail-open, data-loss, or security path counts only when a supported workflow or the kit's own routes reach it, and a rare or contrived path is MINOR at most or dismissed. Its confirming round treats a new finding as BLOCKER or MAJOR only when it is a reachable fail-open, data-loss, or Done-when gap; anything else is MINOR. A finding line bearing the convergence-class tag defined by LLR-311 is filed and counted as one finding under the unchanged verdict grammar.\""," rationale = \"An attended reviewer needs the same reviewed instructions and durable verdict carrier as an unattended review without inheriting its scheduler. Strict rendering and boundary validation prevent a reviewer from receiving incomplete instructions or an unrelated verdict from becoming review history.\""," test_refs = \"TC-333\""," status = \"Approved\""]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-930\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\test\\test-cases.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":3389,"oldLines":9,"newStart":3389,"newLines":9,"lines":[" [test.TC-333]"," verifies = [\"SR-146\", \"SR-154\", \"SR-235\", \"LLR-313\", \"IF-046\", \"IF-047\", \"IF-288\", \"IF-289\"]"," level = \"Integration\"","-method = \"Run test_a_rendered_review_brief_carries_the_kit_claus